From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:41:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Import pre-database screen time history into SQLite

Bump the history database to version 2 and add a usage_meta key/value
table (the v1 rows are kept by onUpgrade). A one-off backfill flag,
history_backfill_v1, is written only after a successful full scan.

refreshHistory() gains fullScan, which scans the whole requested window
instead of shrinking it to the days since the last refresh; this is what
allows a database that already contains today's row to recover older
days from the system usage event log. The migration runs from the
application IO scope and, as a fallback, when the analysis screen opens
(so it also works right after usage access is granted). Historical rows
are still never downgraded.

The analysis screen also gets an explicit 'Re-import system history'
top bar action with a confirmation dialog, which forces a full rebuild.
